meta {
  name: Verify email
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify-email
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "token": "{{verificationToken}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.emailVerified: eq true
}

docs {
  Register emails a verification link, which lands in Mailpit (http://localhost:8025). The link
  ends in ?token=XYZ - copy that token into the verificationToken environment variable. Until this runs, you can log in
  but Workspaces/Create workspace answers 403 EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED.

  Single use: a second run is 400 INVALID_VERIFICATION_TOKEN, as is an expired (24 h) or replaced
  link. An account registered before verification existed has no link yet - run Resend
  verification first.

  The teammate never needs this: accepting an invitation sent to their own address verifies them.
}
